        "title": "[codex] docs(cli): align transcription fallback order",
        "body": "## Summary\n\n- Align `summarize transcriber setup` output with the current automatic transcription order, including Deepgram.\n- Reword `--transcriber` docs/help so it is described as selecting the local transcription stage, not overriding Groq globally.\n- Update README and mode docs to consistently describe the runtime order: Groq first when keyed, then local ONNX/`whisper.cpp`, then AssemblyAI, Gemini, OpenAI, FAL, and Deepgram.\n- Document Gemini and Deepgram transcription model override env vars where provider keys are listed.\n\n## Why\n\nDeepgram was added to the remote fallback chain, but the setup output still ended at FAL. Several docs also still implied local `whisper.cpp` or ONNX was preferred before Groq, and some wording made `--transcriber` sound like a hard provider override even though Groq still runs first when configured.\n\n## Validation\n\n- `pnpm install --frozen-lockfile`\n- `pnpm exec vitest run tests/transcriber-cli.test.ts tests/cli.help.test.ts tests/transcription.whisper.cloud-providers.test.ts tests/transcription-start.test.ts tests/package-bin.test.ts`\n- `pnpm -s typecheck`\n- `pnpm -s check`\n",
